  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/C1/). VERDICT: CURRENT, numbers worse, one premise wrong. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/selection_index.sqlite = 3,385,262,080 B (3.15 GiB; 2.3 GB at filing), page_size 4096, 826,480 pages, auto_vacuum 0, freelist 1,313; fincore 4.3 MB resident (cold again). No VACUUM/prune anywhere (selection_index.py:392 says 'nothing prunes it'). EXPLAIN (read-only): block WHERE path=? -> covering autoindex; test_block WHERE path=? AND name=? -> test_block_by_block; a full covering-index SCAN only on SELECT DISTINCT test_id FROM test_block (touching_test_files :430, speakable_test_files :452 - the opt-in narrow path). So 'missing index -> full scans' is wrong: every point query is indexed; the random reads are B-tree page access on the per-run fold (DELETE ... WHERE test_id=? + executemany INSERT into two B-trees, smart-test:702/1969) and point lookups over a file nothing compacts (about 1 GB/month). open_index (:125-126) sets no PRAGMA (no mmap_size/cache_size). Title re-scoped. ROOT CAUSE: append-only index with no compaction, so cold-cache cost scales with total size, not the query's working set (singleton, CI tooling family). Status unchanged."  # 7ce1
